      "item_body": "<p>Use at least five curve-sketching techniques to explain how to sketch the graph of f(x) = (2x + 10)/(x^2 - 9). Sketch the graph on graph paper.</p>\n<p>discontinuities (vertical asymptotes): <span id=\"blank_7831f274-149d-4dbe-aedb-6bb84b035c69\"></span></p>\n<p>at x = -3, as x -&gt; -3 from the left, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_3151ad3a-eb4f-4ddf-9d55-21893bba2c7e\"></span>; as x -&gt; -3 from the right, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_35eb4284-c6e3-4903-9c3b-cf60e81ff142\"></span></p>\n<p>at x = 3, as x -&gt; 3 from the left, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_b4a4ae02-9c9a-4142-a189-b11305b01b6b\"></span>; as x -&gt; 3 from the right, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_54058538-a178-4874-b483-57c2e3da19fc\"></span></p>\n<p>y-intercept: <span id=\"blank_e240f31c-5701-4251-900b-3baed97145f9\"></span></p>\n<p>x-intercept: <span id=\"blank_e184d78c-d3e0-44ff-b1d7-e13b3ba45937\"></span></p>\n<p>local minimum at (<span id=\"blank_94417b13-25cb-4eab-aff0-9008f99a3262\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_249d4444-e45b-470e-889e-e0c2f4101dd2\"></span>)</p>\n<p>local maximum at (<span id=\"blank_67d00087-9f47-4be4-895b-e139576e4744\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_76853a6b-4694-4046-8aff-225215a26a6f\"></span>)</p>\n<p>horizontal asymptote: <span id=\"blank_82ed6f18-3b92-4a0b-a42f-77a254f47160\"></span></p>\n<p>Sketch the graph of f(x) = (2x + 10)/(x^2 - 9), with vertical asymptotes at x = -3 and x = 3, a horizontal asymptote at y = 0, a y-intercept of -10/9, an x-intercept at -5, a local minimum at (-9, -1/9), and a local maximum at (-1, -1).</p>",
