      "item_body": "<p>For the function f(x) = 5x/(x - 1)^2, show that f'(x) = -5(x + 1)/(x - 1)^3 and f''(x) = 10(x + 2)/(x - 1)^4. Use the function and its derivatives to determine the domain, intercepts, and asymptotes, intervals of increase and decrease, intervals of concavity, local extrema, and points of inflection. Sketch the graph.</p>\n<p>domain: <span id=\"blank_3768fa84-a9a1-41f8-ac77-231a3adfe231\"></span></p>\n<p>x-intercept: <span id=\"blank_9816fe4b-43ee-42a9-afd2-2064e4bea379\"></span></p>\n<p>y-intercept: <span id=\"blank_325af125-d110-4104-95e3-4d39e6d941ce\"></span></p>\n<p>vertical asymptote: <span id=\"blank_c8e62569-d981-4e2a-bd71-5592ee3fe62d\"></span>; as x -&gt; 1 from the left, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_976710a2-e0b1-4d59-a690-a4a384a99ec7\"></span>; as x -&gt; 1 from the right, f(x) -&gt; <span id=\"blank_9e1978c1-2109-4009-a6b8-c4fbb061998d\"></span></p>\n<p>horizontal asymptote: <span id=\"blank_8a1e8df5-1885-4226-9116-3e978a30cb3b\"></span></p>\n<p>increasing on <span id=\"blank_09125c30-e2a4-456a-a8b1-4b74dfb1bd60\"></span></p>\n<p>decreasing on <span id=\"blank_ad95bc21-72e7-45ee-af72-c6a0b3e79874\"></span></p>\n<p>concave down on <span id=\"blank_c8820025-621d-4533-8155-903346b56d13\"></span></p>\n<p>concave up on <span id=\"blank_52a55049-85f0-4131-b802-081ac5847f94\"></span></p>\n<p>local minimum at (<span id=\"blank_b37620a4-600b-424c-a0ad-ef8f9b1523f4\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_3dc27d48-0083-462c-b7f4-f6bb9fa713c8\"></span>)</p>\n<p>point of inflection at (<span id=\"blank_0e194e3c-c678-482d-912f-874dbed77d9c\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_898ac2c1-a453-4491-bc5a-adba5d3a130a\"></span>)</p>\n<p>Sketch the graph of f(x) = 5x/(x - 1)^2, with a vertical asymptote at x = 1, a horizontal asymptote at y = 0, a local minimum at (-1, -1.25), and a point of inflection at (-2, -1.11).</p>",
