      "item_body": "<p>Each graph is the graph of f''(x) for some function f(x). For each graph, determine i. the intervals on which the graph of f(x) is concave up and the intervals on which it is concave down; ii. the x-coordinates of all points of inflection of f(x); iii. a rough sketch of a possible graph of f(x), assuming that f(0) = 2.</p>\n<p><img id=\"55750\" src=\"https://inst-fs-iad-prod.inscloudgate.net/files/dab45266-ee3f-474b-bdf2-0b8c3b15f5f2/ex44_q5.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsImtpZCI6Im5ldy1xdWl6emVzL21haW4ifQ..G2IHdunuUe_ST7byhim5SNweHZecpiV8-SmJt1Cw8AqIkykktomwQoi71cuJWrviwGxpQGc5rb7IfBiY72s2sg\" alt=\"ex44_q5.png\" data-old-link=\"/courses/905/files/55750/preview\"></p>\n<p>a. i. concave up on <span id=\"blank_4a9038fc-67d8-4037-9322-95531f05c074\"></span>; concave down on <span id=\"blank_0e365ac5-1764-4565-8f95-7bb2ae8f38a9\"></span></p>\n<p>a. ii. point of inflection at <span id=\"blank_887cdd77-e316-415a-b9b5-1cbd2cfd7f2a\"></span></p>\n<p>a. iii. Sketch a possible graph of f(x) with f(0) = 2, concave up before x = 1 and concave down after, with an inflection point at x = 1.</p>\n<p>b. i. concave up on <span id=\"blank_1fb8c5ef-56ee-4bd2-b433-b1ca48cd723c\"></span>; concave down on <span id=\"blank_606a0731-f58f-4b31-9d2c-779f4dddb5d8\"></span></p>\n<p>b. ii. points of inflection at <span id=\"blank_5adf2ae2-b87b-4012-88df-8c5ffbf83e48\"></span></p>\n<p>b. iii. Sketch a possible graph of f(x) with f(0) = 2, concave up on x &lt; 0 and x &gt; 2 and concave down on 0 &lt; x &lt; 2, with inflection points at x = 0 and x = 2.</p>",
